Tenant has moved out. Here is what is to expect next... 

Due to the potential for foundation movement in the area, we first send an engineer to measure and inspect the house for foundation movement. This is done at no cost to you.

We will also perform a hydrostatic test at no cost to you.  This is a test in which the drain pipes underground and in the slab can be tested for leaks. The pipes are plugged/sealed and filled with water.  Any changes in the water level indicates a possible issue and further plumbing work might be needed.

We will assess the property and make a list of repairs needed to get the property back into rent ready condition. We must wait to proceed on this list though, as it will be dependent on whether foundation repairs or further plumbing repairs are needed.

We understand that time is of the essence for you and we will make every attempt to quickly get the engineer and hydrostatic results back.  This process usually takes 7-10 days but can take up to two weeks depending on contractor availability and scheduling.  The turn around time for all of this to occur is around 10 days from the initial notification of the vacancy.  Although this is a timely process, it is the right way to do this.  This will ensure that there are no bigger issues moving forward and will prepare the property for tenancy.


Thank you,
Rehab Department